cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Odd-Support Resource: Tournament Parity under Incomplete Competition"
abstract: >-
  Tournament-generation engine and analysis code for the paper "Reproducing the
  Odd-Support Invariant and its Incompleteness Limit: A Bridge from Tournament
  Parity Theory to the Allesina-Levine Ecological Model." Measures how structural
  sparsity, competitive neutrality, complementarity breaking, and the number of
  limiting factors perturb the odd-support parity of zero-sum tournaments in the
  Allesina-Levine factor-rank model, and ties the resulting U-shaped
  support-versus-connectivity curve to the Pfaffian / perfect-matching mechanism.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aho"
    given-names: "Matti"
    affiliation: "Aalto University"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/MattiAAho/odd-support-resource"
url: "https://github.com/MattiAAho/odd-support-resource"
keywords:
  - "tournament parity"
  - "odd-support invariant"
  - "zero-sum games"
  - "Pfaffian"
  - "perfect matching"
  - "species coexistence"
  - "theoretical ecology"
